@@ -74,7 +74,13 @@ CREATE IMAGE IMAGE_SIZE CHARS ALLOT \ This space contains the target image.
 \ bisection, not fully root-caused - see PROGRESS.md). These are called
 \ often enough, from enough different contexts, that avoiding DO/LOOP's
 \ own return-stack usage entirely was the safer fix.
+\ (experiment) a cell of the target is a cell of this host when the sizes match
+\ and this host is little-endian - the byte loops below give the same bytes
+VARIABLE FAST-T
+: FAST-T? ( --- )  1 PAD ! PAD C@ 1 =  TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ 1 CELLS = AND FAST-T ! ;
+FAST-T?
 : @-T  ( t-addr --- x)
+  FAST-T @ IF CHARS IMAGE + @ EXIT THEN
   0 0
   BEGIN
     DUP TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ <
@@ -97,6 +103,7 @@ CREATE IMAGE IMAGE_SIZE CHARS ALLOT \ This space contains the target image.
     THEN
   THEN ;
 : !-T  ( x t-addr ---)
